# Example fixture: Si(111) slab, 4 layers + vacuum (32 atoms), cut via
# pymatgen.core.surface.SlabGenerator (the same generator stb-slab uses)
# from bulk diamond-cubic Si (a=5.43 Ang), termination index 0 (the
# non-polar/symmetric one pymatgen sorts first). Each of the 8 surface
# atoms is missing exactly 1 bond (coordination 3 instead of the bulk
# value 4) -- confirmed the missing-bond direction recovered by
# stb-passivate's vector-sum method sits at exactly 109.47 deg from the
# existing bonds (the ideal tetrahedral angle). Used to exercise the
# straightforward auto-passivation path (expect 8 H atoms added, 40 total,
# no "needs manual attention" warning).

NumberOfSpecies    1
NumberofAtoms      32

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   14   Si
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 5.43000000   0.00000000   -5.43000000
 -0.00000000   5.43000000   -5.43000000
 0.00000000   0.00000000   43.44000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  0.00000000   0.50000000   0.32812500   1
  0.25000000   0.25000000   0.29687500   1
